.TH tujoin n 0.23.0 tclutils "Tcl Library Procedures"
.SH NAME
tujoin \-  tclutils::tujoin  joins two simple delimited text sources on a selected
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
package require tclutils::tujoin
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
set left  "1;Ada\en2;Linus\en"
set right "1;Berlin\en2;Helsinki\en"

::tclutils::tujoin::texts $left $right \-delimiter ";"
# \-> 1;Ada;Berlin
# \-> 2;Linus;Helsinki
.fi
.PP
Options:
.PP
.nf
\-delimiter ";"
\-leftfield 1
\-rightfield 1
\-joiner ";"
\-header 0
.fi
.PP
Field numbers are 1\-based. The joined result contains the key once, then the
.PP
remaining left fields, then the remaining right fields.

